think The live green edge is the Season G SCENE-READ family (208 image modules). The newest laps closed the single-click gesture: click_expand (point->group), click_facts (point->group facts), click_bounds (point->group frame). The crux-completion is the TWO-click read -- what a PAIR of taps means together, the relation a surface answers when a keeper taps two things.
think Verified the composition API before building: hit_test.object_label_at (PointOutOfBounds off-map, 0 on a background miss), overlap_clusters.cluster_of (object label -> dense group id), cluster_adjacency.cluster_distance (true nearest-pixel Chebyshev gap, floored at 2, refuses SameCluster) and cluster_frames_overlap. Reused the click_facts chain scene (A/B/C one connected group {1,2,3}, far singleton D) so one scene carries all three crux shapes.
think Designed image/click_relation.rye: click_group_id (a tap's group, EmptyClick on a miss), click_pair_same_group, click_pair_distance (0 when same group, else cluster_distance), click_pair_frames_overlap (SameGroup refusal on one group). Computed the geometry by hand: min chain-to-D pair gap 3 via B's (4,8) to D's (1,11); clicked-pixel distances 8 (A->D) vs 7 (C->D) differ while the group gap is one number 3; chain frame (1,1)-(11,11) and D frame (0,11)-(1,12) meet on both axes so frames_overlap TRUE while members sit 3 apart.
obs GREEN on the FIRST full metal run, no code reds. The only correction was a TAME ban: two compound asserts (assert(a and b)) split into single asserts -- caught by tame_style_check before commit, exactly the check's job. The crux is the exact lift of cluster_adjacency's cluster-pair reads from two cluster IDs to two POINTS: the relation belongs to the groups the taps expand to, invariant to where within each group a keeper taps.
